# Self-signed certificates from Caddy's own internal CA instead of public
# ACME, for every site block. Use only for local development or CI/Docker
# test environments that have no real DNS resolution or reachable port
# 80/443 for a real ACME challenge - browsers and non-Caddy HTTP clients
# will not trust these certs unless they also trust Caddy's local root
# (curl needs -k, or --cacert against the exported root). Never select this
# on a real production origin: it silently produces certificates the public
# internet cannot verify.
local_certs
